    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nHello! When MiniPick is launched with a custom command which **doesn't** exist, it spits out the following error on picker close:\n\n```\nError in User Autocommands for \"MiniPickStop\":\nLua callback: ...hare/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:1795: attempt to index upvalue 'process' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        ...hare/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:1795: in function <...hare/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:1791>\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec_autocmds'\n        ...hare/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:2708: in function 'picker_stop'\n        ...hare/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua:2298: in function 'cli'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Forget to install `fd`.\n2. Launch MiniPicker: `:lua MiniPick.builtin.cli({ command = { 'fd' } })`\n3. Close the empty picker with Esc.",
